  "notes": "Compound of {鼓|こ} (drum; to rouse) + {舞|ぶ} (dance). The imagery is of beating drums and dancing to raise morale — an ancient military practice.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {士気|しき}を{鼓舞|こぶ}する (boost morale)\n- チームを{鼓舞|こぶ}する (rally a team)\n- {自|みずか}らを{鼓舞|こぶ}する (motivate oneself)\n- {鼓舞|こぶ}{激励|げきれい} (encouragement and rallying)\n\nUSAGE:\nMore formal and literary than {励|はげ}ます (to encourage). {鼓舞|こぶ}する implies rousing someone's fighting spirit or passion, while {励|はげ}ます is gentler and more supportive. Often appears in sports, military, and leadership contexts.",
